        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Iran says 'no decision' on joining new talks, with US delegation set to depart Middle East Issued on: 20/04/2026 - 20:13 Modified: 20/04/2026 - 20:22 Iran said it had yet to decide whether to attend a new round of peace negotiations with the United States, as Washington's delegation prepared to depart for Pakistan on Monday. The uncertainty over the talks on ending the war that engulfed the region came as US President Donald Trump suggested he could resume attacks should the current temporary ceasefire -- now in its final days -- lapse. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran. 'Trump has boxed himself into a corner', expert says as fate of Iran peace talks uncertain 20/04/2026 Middle East 'Hierarchy of sovereignty': Israel claims authority over 'which Lebanese areas are inhabitable' 20/04/2026 Middle East US seizes Iranian-flagged cargo ship 20/04/2026 Middle East 'US military leverage a risky tactic': Bombs, military escalation will not bring Iran 'to the table' 20/04/2026 Middle East Trump sending US delegation for Iran talks in Pakistan 19/04/2026 Middle East 'Ceasefire in the Middle East, especially in Lebanon, are meant to be broken', analyst says 19/04/2026 Middle East Iran asserts leverage in Hormuz ahead of new round of talks 19/04/2026 Middle East Israel's double game between negotiations with Lebanon and occupation in the south 19/04/2026 Middle East Food security under threat as Middle East war disrupts fertiliser supply 19/04/2026 Middle East"
